The series is arranged alphabetically by subject headings. The index begins with a list of primary subject headings, as well as secondary headings. A detailed index follows. The index provides reference to the file numbers that were assigned in 1988 to manage the correspondence of the Queen Victoria Medical Centre (VA1254).<br />
<br />
The file number is assigned according to the year the file was assigned to its box, then the box number itself, and lastly the file&rsquo;s position in the box. For example, file number &#39;88.1.0&#39; refers to the file being assigned a box in 1988, in box number 1, in the first position in the box. &nbsp;

function_content:
This series comprises newsletters created to inform hospital staff in matters relevant to the Queen Victoria Medical Centre (VA 1254). Five different newsletters were published over different periods and were printed as pamphlets. They were titled &ldquo;The Family Hospital&rdquo;, &ldquo;Staff Newsletter&rdquo;, &ldquo;Centre News&rdquo;, &ldquo;QV Quarterly&rdquo; and &ldquo;Queen Vic News&rdquo;.<br />
<br />
&nbsp;

This series comprises annual reports for the Royal Park Psychiatric Hospital (VA 2845).<br />
&nbsp;<br />
The annual reports provide a summary of the activities of the hospital for each year including statistics relating to those activities. In addition they provide reports from the different departments, as well as annual financial statements.&nbsp;

This series comprises reports of the public section of the Obstetrics and Paediatrics department of the Essendon and District Memorial Hospital (VA 1247).<br />
<br />
The reports provide a statistical summary of the work of the public unit, including numbers of specific medical procedures undertaken and conditions treated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

This series comprises the meeting minutes of the Committee of Management of The Royal Melbourne Hospital and Associated Hospitals School of Nursing (VA 5263).<br />
<br />
The Committee of Management was the prime decision making body and the group responsible for the overall management of the School from its establishment in 1950 until its closure in 1963.&nbsp;

This series consists of By-Laws of the Western and North Western Health Care Network, North West Hospital, Western Hospital, Williamstown Hospital, Altona District Hospital and the North Eastern Health Care Network.<br />
&nbsp;<br />
The By-Laws define the powers and responsibilities of the Board of Management, Chief Executive Officer, Sub-committees, and the rules on the use of the Seal, financial matters, auditors, Annual General Meetings, disposal of assets, intellectual property, delegations, and tendering for building works. The series contains finalised By-Laws, drafts of proposed By-Laws, sample By-Laws from other institutions and correspondence about the drafting of the By-Laws.&nbsp;

