This series is arranged in an annual single number system with a sequential number for each case followed by the year (i.e., 1/1929), described as a Case Number.<br />
<br />
&nbsp;

This series is arranged in an annual single number system with a sequential number for each case followed by the year (i.e., 1/1929), described as a Case Number.<br />
<br />
From 1929 to 1944, cases from Camperdown, Terang, Cobden, and Mortlake courts were registered using a single recordkeeping system. After this time, Terang, Cobden and Mortlake courts began using their own registers (VPRS 19506, VPRS 19502 and VPRS 19504 respectively). The Case details from the combined register (VPRS 19501) were copied into these new registers and are notated as such.&nbsp;

